  "id": "COMPOUND:26728 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (1R,4R)-4-Hydroxydauca-7-Ene-6,9-Dione and Phosphodiesterase 6C, as this compound is identified as a target of multiple entities that ultimately interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C. Specifically, the compound is linked to HaCaT cells, which are targeted by Melodinine D and 6-O-Veratroylcatalpol, both of which have Phosphodiesterase 6C as a downstream target. Additionally, the compound is associated with HaCaT cells, which are also targeted by Gemcitabine elaidate, another compound that interacts with Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings collectively indicate that (1R,4R)-4-Hydroxydauca-7-Ene-6,9-Dione may play a role in modulating Phosphodiesterase 6C activity through its interaction with downstream targets in the signaling pathways of HaCaT cells. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, suggesting a possible functional relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
